00:13:56.193 --> 00:13:58.643
- (speaking Amharic)

00:13:58.643 --> 00:13:59.870
- Usually a lot of people do it,

00:13:59.870 --> 00:14:01.600
like it's not a one person job.

00:14:01.600 --> 00:14:03.440
We just sit and all fold it together.

00:14:03.440 --> 00:14:05.963
- I feel like I'm the slowest person.

00:14:05.963 --> 00:14:08.340
- (speaking Amharic)

00:14:08.340 --> 00:14:09.403
- That's the glue?

00:14:10.534 --> 00:14:12.470
- (speaking Amharic)

00:14:12.470 --> 00:14:14.043
- It is mostly skin.

00:14:14.043 --> 00:14:16.710
(both laughing)

00:14:18.595 --> 00:14:19.475
- I have no idea what I'm-

00:14:19.475 --> 00:14:21.290
- (speaking Amharic)

00:14:21.290 --> 00:14:22.123
- Is it good?

00:14:22.123 --> 00:14:25.876
- (speaking Amharic)

00:14:25.876 --> 00:14:27.165
- Are you sure?

00:14:27.165 --> 00:14:29.050
- (speaking Amharic)

00:14:29.050 --> 00:14:30.810
- Isn't it too flat though?

00:14:30.810 --> 00:14:34.728
I'm going to try a few
more, until I get it right.

00:14:34.728 --> 00:14:36.260
- (speaking Amharic)

00:14:36.260 --> 00:14:38.909
- Look how much progress I made.

00:14:38.909 --> 00:14:43.130
This one almost no filling,
this is my first try.

00:14:43.130 --> 00:14:45.264
And now, I know how to stuff.

00:14:45.264 --> 00:14:48.347
- (speaking Amharic)

00:14:52.490 --> 00:14:53.493
- Set aside.

00:14:55.270 --> 00:14:57.170
I think we have to fry right?

00:14:57.170 --> 00:14:58.003
- We do.

00:14:58.003 --> 00:14:59.328
- In oil?

00:14:59.328 --> 00:15:02.411
- (speaking Amharic)

00:15:10.179 --> 00:15:11.480
- 375?

00:15:11.480 --> 00:15:12.313
- Less.

00:15:12.313 --> 00:15:13.539
- 365.

00:15:13.539 --> 00:15:14.372
- 350.

00:15:14.372 --> 00:15:15.205
- 350. I'm sorry!

00:15:18.500 --> 00:15:21.720
We gotta wait until this reaches 350.

00:15:21.720 --> 00:15:23.907
- Yeah, but you have
to say 350 in Amharic.

00:15:23.907 --> 00:15:26.824
(speaking Amharic)

00:15:30.250 --> 00:15:31.637
- Okay, it's 350.

00:15:32.957 --> 00:15:36.040
- (speaking Amharic)

00:15:38.360 --> 00:15:40.017
- Like three? No, four.

00:15:47.192 --> 00:15:49.610
- (speaking Amharic)

00:15:49.610 --> 00:15:52.953
- Until golden brown? Five minutes?

00:15:57.130 --> 00:15:58.170
Sounds funny.

00:15:58.170 --> 00:16:01.400
- They're talking.
They're speaking Amharic.

00:16:11.227 --> 00:16:12.060
- (speaking Amharic)

00:16:12.060 --> 00:16:13.347
- Oh, drain the oil.

00:16:13.347 --> 00:16:16.430
- (speaking Amharic)

00:16:17.390 --> 00:16:18.688
- Another four?

00:16:18.688 --> 00:16:21.150
- (speaking Amharic)

00:16:21.150 --> 00:16:22.703
- Okay, do everything.

00:16:27.536 --> 00:16:28.540
- Okay, (Amharic) is six.

00:16:28.540 --> 00:16:30.103
- A new number.

00:16:30.963 --> 00:16:33.110
- Is Mimo a popular name?

00:16:33.110 --> 00:16:35.650
- No, I think Mimi is popular,

00:16:35.650 --> 00:16:38.640
but my grandmother called
me Mimo when I was little.

00:16:38.640 --> 00:16:41.300
And then it stayed. That's
actually not my real name.

00:16:41.300 --> 00:16:42.630
- Oh, what's your real name?

00:16:42.630 --> 00:16:45.897
- It's Bemnat, Bemnat is my real name,

00:16:45.897 --> 00:16:49.743
but we have house names,
and my house name was Mimo.

00:16:49.743 --> 00:16:53.767
Because it's like my, my
little girl, so my grandma-.

00:16:53.767 --> 00:16:55.140
- Oh, so it's kinda nickname.

00:16:55.140 --> 00:16:58.060
- Yeah, but then it's
like now my actual name.

00:16:58.060 --> 00:17:01.060
It's normal for little
lentils to come out.

00:17:01.060 --> 00:17:01.893
- All right.

00:17:02.833 --> 00:17:05.984
- (speaking Amharic)

00:17:05.984 --> 00:17:08.403
- Okay, I'm assuming, just plate?

00:17:09.464 --> 00:17:12.547
- (speaking Amharic)

00:17:16.803 --> 00:17:18.303
- This is nothing.

00:17:20.119 --> 00:17:22.310
- (speaking Amharic)

00:17:22.310 --> 00:17:24.250
- I'll go get mine, wanna compare?

00:17:24.250 --> 00:17:25.618
- Okay, yes.

00:17:25.618 --> 00:17:26.451
- All right, I'll be back.

00:17:26.451 --> 00:17:27.333
You ready?

00:17:29.655 --> 00:17:31.570
- Aww, yours so pretty!

00:17:31.570 --> 00:17:34.722
- You did really good, I'm impressed.

00:17:34.722 --> 00:17:35.555
- Thank you!

00:17:35.555 --> 00:17:36.555
I think I did great.

00:17:39.040 --> 00:17:40.870
I had no idea what she was talking about,

00:17:40.870 --> 00:17:42.410
but I did my best.

00:17:42.410 --> 00:17:44.840
- I'm excited, it looks crunchy.

00:17:44.840 --> 00:17:45.760
- Let's try yours first.

00:17:45.760 --> 00:17:47.560
- All right, I'm gonna try this one.

00:17:50.122 --> 00:17:54.300
- Mmm, it's good. Are
you gonna be making this?

00:17:54.300 --> 00:17:58.600
- Yeah, it was easy if it
was English or Japanese.

00:17:58.600 --> 00:17:59.600
- Yeah, for sure.

00:17:59.600 --> 00:18:01.050
- And this is vegetarian.

00:18:01.050 --> 00:18:04.250
- Yeah, it is. We usually
make it with lentils.

00:18:04.250 --> 00:18:07.070
Other cultures make it with ground beef.

00:18:07.070 --> 00:18:09.720
So we call this in Ethiopia, sambusa.

00:18:09.720 --> 00:18:12.410
- Sambusa. It almost sounds like samosa.

00:18:12.410 --> 00:18:14.770
- I don't know where the
translation got lost,

00:18:14.770 --> 00:18:16.602
but we pronounce it sambusa.

00:18:16.602 --> 00:18:19.680
But it's the same as
samosa. You wanna try mine?

00:18:19.680 --> 00:18:20.694
- Yeah!

00:18:20.694 --> 00:18:22.000
- Let's do it.

00:18:22.000 --> 00:18:23.173
- So cute.

00:18:25.600 --> 00:18:28.673
I like yours filled a lot of filling,

00:18:28.673 --> 00:18:33.673
like I was struggling filling
inside, but this is plump.

00:18:34.474 --> 00:18:36.000
- Yeah, most of the time
you learn how to make this

00:18:36.000 --> 00:18:38.141
when you're little, cause
it's a family activity.

00:18:38.141 --> 00:18:40.277
And your mom would be frying it,

00:18:40.277 --> 00:18:42.010
and the kids would be folding it,

00:18:42.010 --> 00:18:44.350
so I've been doing this
since I was very little.

00:18:44.350 --> 00:18:45.183
- Oh wow.

00:18:45.183 --> 00:18:47.125
- But you're getting
started now, so one day,

00:18:47.125 --> 00:18:50.093
yours will be as fluffy as mine.

00:18:52.016 --> 00:18:54.250
- Yes. Thank you so much
for teaching me Amharic,

00:18:54.250 --> 00:18:56.520
and thank you so much for
teaching me how to cook

00:18:56.520 --> 00:18:57.470
sambusa.

00:18:57.470 --> 00:18:59.576
- You're so welcome, thanks for learning.

00:18:59.576 --> 00:19:02.480
- Thank you, and thank you guys!

00:19:02.480 --> 00:19:04.142
Follow me on my journey!

00:19:04.142 --> 00:19:05.173
(both) Ciao!

00:19:07.150 --> 00:19:08.233
- [Man] Oh, yes!

00:19:09.616 --> 00:19:12.366
(cheerful music)

